  "cipher_explanation": "An intelligent system need not maintain a complete high-fidelity representation of everything it has encountered. It may instead preserve symbolic guideposts, relational constraints, coordinates, attractors, and retrieval pointers that define a navigable representation of the underlying information. Reasoning proceeds as coherent descent through this symbolic structure. Memory becomes coordinate navigation and local reconstruction rather than complete archival playback. In conversation, independent observers may alter one another's reachable symbolic spaces until their coherent paths enter a common destination class. The relevant transition is therefore a Convergence Boundary: a condition in which path selection may remain variable while coherent destination selection becomes constrained."
